wip-mach
========

wip-mach is a new kernel, written from scratch in Rust. It is free
software under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or, at your
option, any later version (LICENCES/GPL-2.0.txt).

It is inspired by GNU Mach, the microkernel of the GNU Hurd, at commit
c5701c1c1c8f330f7a790a4a0bc6b3434213722b of
<https://git.savannah.gnu.org/git/hurd/gnumach.git>. wip-mach
reproduces GNU Mach's interface to user space, and much of its code
was written by reading GNU Mach's: its algorithms, its data structures
and its behaviour.

wip-mach is a fully new implementation, but it was not made in a clean
room. Its files were written, split, merged and rewritten with GNU
Mach's sources open, so no file of wip-mach corresponds to one file of
GNU Mach, and it is not possible to say that a file of one is directly
related to a file of the other. The work as a whole is therefore
treated as derived from GNU Mach, and the respect owed to GNU Mach's
authors is kept here, in this single file, rather than in each source
file. A source file that draws on an upstream says so in one line,

    // Inspired by GNU Mach; see COPYRIGHT.

and carries the copyright of its own authors only.


GNU Mach
--------

Upstream: <https://git.savannah.gnu.org/git/hurd/gnumach.git>,
commit c5701c1c1c8f330f7a790a4a0bc6b3434213722b.

GNU Mach descends from Mach 3.0 of Carnegie Mellon University, through
